    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01JK8RJN5F77E90RA9V8GRBNEE\">You will learn </h2>\n<p>Learn how to share reviews between 2 or more of your storefronts, also called multi-store syndication. This is helpful if you have multiple storefronts for different locations, but sell some or all of the same products in each. </p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JK8RJN5F8M3S00XCH911DYD2\">Requirements </h2>\n<p>In order to configure multi-store syndication, all accounts must be part of the same portfolio. <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/24656917054747\">Set up a portfolio</a> containing all the accounts you’d like to syndicate before proceeding. A Klaviyo account can only be a part of one syndication group, but a portfolio may contain multiple groups. Adding an account to a syndication group will remove it from any other syndication group it is currently part of. </p>\n<p>A maximum of 10 Klaviyo accounts can be syndicated at one time. </p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JK8RJN5FC67TGT9MNG2W25RE\">About syndicating reviews to other stores </h2>\n<p>Multi-store syndication allows you to share reviews across products hosted on different storefronts. Syndication is two-way, meaning all reviews from every syndicated account will appear in reviews widgets for all other syndicated accounts. Reviews will be ordered based on each account’s <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/28858764961947\">language and translation settings</a>. </p>\n<p>Reviews are mapped between accounts based on unique SKUs. This means every store you intend to syndicate should use the same SKUs for matching products. </p>\n<p>Reviews must be <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/19351110471323\">moderated</a> from the account where they were originally submitted. You cannot approve a review in one syndicated account, but reject it in another. Reviews will only appear in your Klaviyo reviews dashboard in the account where the review originated.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JK8RJN5FR4XWZX48F5K8K7E2\">Enable review syndication</h2>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>After completing this process, reviews will begin appearing across all selected storefronts within 1 week. </p>\n</div>\n<ol>\n<li>From an account you’d like to syndicate, navigate to <strong>Reviews</strong>. </li>\n<li>Select <strong>Reviews settings</strong>. </li>\n<li>Select <strong>Syndication</strong>.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/33625718938139\" alt=\"\" width=\"450\" height=\"273\">\n</li>\n<li>In the <em>Multi-store</em> section, toggle on the setting <strong>Syndicate reviews to other stores</strong>.</li>\n<li>Select the account(s) that should share reviews with the one you’re currently logged in to. You can only syndicate reviews between accounts where you are an owner or an admin; if you don’t have sufficient access, ask your Klaviyo account administrator to upgrade your access in all accounts you’d like to syndicate. </li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save changes</strong>. </li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JK8RJN5FFS09BM1GY9BAKX0B\">Disable review syndication</h2>\n<p>If you’d like to remove syndication after setting it up, there are 2 options: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove a single store from a syndicated group </li>\n<li>Disable syndication for the entire group</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>You must be an admin or owner for every account in the syndicated group in order to disable syndication entirely. </p>\n</div>\n<p>To remove a single store from a syndicated group: </p>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to a different Klaviyo account within the syndicated group. This process cannot be completed within the account you are removing.</li>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Reviews</strong>. </li>\n<li>Select <strong>Reviews settings</strong>. </li>\n<li>Select <strong>Syndication</strong>. </li>\n<li>In the <em>Multi-store</em> section, deselect the account you’d like to remove from the syndicated group. </li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save changes</strong>. <br>\n<p>To disable syndication for an entire group:</p>\n</li>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Reviews</strong> from any account in the syndication group. </li>\n<li>Select <strong>Reviews settings</strong>. </li>\n<li>Select <strong>Syndication</strong>. </li>\n<li>In the <em>Multi-store</em> section, toggle off the setting <strong>Syndicate reviews to other stores</strong>. </li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save changes</strong>. </li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JK8RJN5F748DXTTSERYGP44X\">Outcome </h2>\n<p>Once you enable multi-store syndication, reviews will begin appearing across all selected storefronts within 1 week. </p>",
